LICENSE MAP

This repository holds four editions of "Structure and Interpretation
of Computer Programs" (Abelson, Sussman, and Sussman), adapted to
Rust, OCaml, TypeScript, and Kotlin. The files fall under one of four
licenses by path. The full texts are in the LICENSES/ directory.

Text, figures, and exercise statements: CC BY-SA 4.0
  text/assets/css/           the book stylesheets (fonts below excepted)
  */book/                    the adapted prose of each edition
  text/original/figures/     the SVG figures and their PDF renderings
  LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Programs: GPL-3.0-only
  */examples/                every listing that appears in the text
  */exercises/               the pending scaffolds
  */solutions/               the reference solutions
  */appendix/                the OCaml Base and Core appendix code
  spec/host-subsets/         the conformance corpus
  LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt
  Listings that correspond to programs printed in the book are Adapted
  Material under CC BY-SA 4.0 Section 1(a). GPLv3 is the BY-SA
  Compatible License that Section 3(b)(1) permits for Adapted Material
  (declared by Creative Commons on 2015-10-08, version 3 only), and it
  is chosen for the original code in the same trees so that each tree
  has one license.

Tooling and site: MIT
  tools/                     the Python build scripts
  site/                      the landing page
  justfile, */justfile, .github/
  LICENSES/MIT.txt

Fonts: SIL Open Font License 1.1
  text/assets/css/fonts/     Linux Libertine, Linux Biolinum,
                             Inconsolata LGC, DejaVu, STIX
  text/assets/css/fonts/OFL-1.1.txt and LICENCE.txt

Prior modification record
  LICENSE.src                the GPL-3.0 notice of the upstream build
                             scripts, retained unchanged

The prose may be reused under CC BY-SA 4.0 and the code under
GPL-3.0-only; the two never mix in one file. Attribution and the
modification statement are in NOTICE.md.
